NSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "___________ is a condition in which sac will travel through the fibrous tissue", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 511, "answer": {"text": ": Subcutaneous Hernia", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "The ____________ is referred to as semilunar line.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 595, "answer": {"text": "Spigelian Line", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "______________ in most of the cases lays the foundation for the Hernia sacs,", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 651, "answer": {"text": "Peritoneum", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": ".Often, it is difficult to diagnose because the symptoms can be more\n___________ in nature.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 733, "answer": {"text": "Non-specific", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "The appendix is usually a component of ___________.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 829, "answer": {"text": "Abdominal Hernias", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "bb9b7c303f8ade32-p6", "label": "Part B · READING 22.pdf", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "bb9b7c303f8ade320d17f4a77968f8856a1236fb4b48b50a3e8397609a619342", "pages": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "questions": [{"number": 3, "prompt": "What the given notice indicate:?\nRole of key players in the immunologic antitumor response\nRole of key players is not completely known\nRole of metabolism\nCancer cells\nCancer cells reprogram their metabolism to rely primarily on glycolysis even in the\npresence of oxygen. This shift to aerobic glycolysis with lactate production, which\nis referred to as the Warburg effect, is now emerging as a hallmark of cancer. The\naltered metabolism allows cancer cells to convert efficiently glucose into\nmacromolecules needed to sustain higher proliferative rates and consequently\nresults in lactate accumulation in the tumor microenvironment. Currently, lactate is\nregarded as a tumor-promoting factor. Lactate accumulation in tumors has been\nassociated with higher incidence of metastases as well as an overall reduced\nsurvival rate of the cancer patients. Previous work has strongly implicated that\nlactate is able to suppress antitumor immunity through inactivation of cytotoxic T\nlymphocytes. However, it is uncertain how the function goes on.", "sourcePage": 8, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": ": Role of key players in the immunologic antitumor response", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "What is correct, according to the figure?\nOnly six of 42 patients contacted on day 7 (14.3%) reported increased pain\n7â€‰days after BFA treatment.\nThe meanÂ±SD pain scores at the start were 7.3Â±2.0.\nAt day 1 and day 7, the mean pain scores were 4.4+2.4â€‰and 5.7Â±2.6,", "sourcePage": 9, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": ": The meanÂ±SD pain scores at the start were 7.3Â±2.0.", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "What is correct as per the given notice?\nthree has been some improvement in the way the patients used to take health\nmedine\ntreatment by effective means have decreased mortality rate\nNutrient restriction has got the potential to change signaling routes.\nGlioblastoma (GBM)\nGlioblastoma (GBM) is a highly aggressive brain tumor and the most commonly\noccurring primary malignant glioma in adults, accounting for approximately 50%\nof all primary malignant brain tumor diagnoses. Standard of care consists of\nsurgical resection, concurrent radiation and chemotherapy, followed by adjuvant\nchemotherapy. While this treatment has extended the average survival to 14.6\nmonths and increased 2 year survival to 17%, the overall prognosis still remains\npoor. GBM has proven difficult to treat due to tumor heterogeneity and the\npresence of tumor microenvironments such as low pH, oxygen, and nutrients\nInitially described as the Warburg Effect, tumor cells can activate alternative\nmetabolic pathways for production of ATP and biomolecules to circumvent\nmicroenvironmental obstacles and fuel tumor growth. Nutrient restriction, just as\nin many cases that we discover understand that is a modulator of the cellular\nmetabolic state and can alter the kinase signaling pathways in the cell, with glucose\nplaying a key role as a precursor for protein, nucleic acid, and lipid synthesis.", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": ": Nutrient restriction has got the potential to change signaling routes.", "source": {"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 22.pdf", "sha256": "b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/b7dc1e74e666dafd6abb0247a25b67ce9fa1285f9b1a707b9efbba33fe341dba.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "bb9b7c303f8ade32-p14", "label": "Part C · READING 22.pdf", "